@startuml
title Account Creation & Crypto Key Setup

actor User
participant Browser
participant "Crypto Module" as Crypto
participant "Local Storage\n(IndexedDB)" as LS
participant Server
database Database

== Account Creation (Traditional) ==
User -> Browser: Create account (username + password)
Browser -> Server: POST /auth/register
Server -> Database: store(username, password_hash)

alt Registration successful
  Server -> Browser: account created
else Username taken
  Server -> Browser: error
end

== Account Login ==
User -> Browser: Login (username + password)
Browser -> Server: POST /auth/login
Server -> Database: verify credentials
Server -> Browser: account session token

== Crypto Key Setup (Authenticated) ==
User -> Browser: Setup crypto keys + passphrase
Browser -> Crypto: generateKeyPair()
Crypto -> Crypto: encryptPrivateKey(passphrase)

Browser -> User: Choose key storage mode

alt Local-only key mode (Recommended)
  Crypto -> LS: store(encryptedPrivateKey)
else Cloud-backed key mode (Optional)
  Crypto -> LS: store(encryptedPrivateKey)
  Browser -> Server: POST /auth/crypto/enable-backup\n(requires account session)
  Server -> Database: storeEncryptedKey()
end

Browser -> Server: POST /auth/crypto/upload-key\n(requires account session)
Server -> Database: store(account_id, publicKey)

note right of Server
Account security (password) is separate
from crypto security (private keys)
end note

@enduml
